==Results==
[[Image:Volba prezidenta.jpg|350px|thumb|Joint session of the Parliament of the Czech Republic electing the President.]]

===First attempt (8–9 February)===
The joint session started on 8 February 2008 at 10 a.m.<ref>{{Cite web | title = Czech Chamber, Senate start session to elect new president |publisher=ČeskéNoviny.cz | url=http://www.ceskenoviny.cz/news/index_view.php?id=295650 | accessdate = 20 February 2008 | year = 2008 }}</ref> As predicted, the vote was delayed by a long debate on the election method, but after six hours it was agreed to hold an open ballot.<ref>{{Cite web | title = Procedure dispute puts Czech presidential election on hold | url= http://earthtimes.org/articles/show/184578.html | accessdate = 20 February 2008 | year = 2008 }}</ref> After two rounds of voting, the session was adjourned at 9 p.m as previously agreed, and the election was postponed to the next day, when the results of the second vote held on the first day were also announced.<ref>{{Cite web | title = 142 for Klaus, 135 for Svejnar in 2nd round of Czech elections |publisher=ČeskéNoviny.cz | url= http://www.ceskenoviny.cz/news/index_view.php?id=295847 | accessdate = 20 February 2008 | year = 2008 }}</ref>

Prior to the third round of voting, three lawmakers left the joint session due to health issues: ČSSD deputy [[Evžen Snítilý]] and KDU-ČSL senators [[Josef Kalbáč]] and [[Karel Barták]].<ref>{{Cite web | title = Another Czech lawmaker out of presidential election |publisher=ČeskéNoviny.cz | url=http://www.ceskenoviny.cz/news/index_view.php?id=295868 | accessdate = 20 February 2008 | year = 2008 }}</ref> Snítilý was thought to be in favour of Švejnar, but supported Klaus in the second election on 15 February and was later expelled from the Social Democrat group, while both Kalbáč and Barták supported Klaus. The third round also failed to produce a winner; the Communists abstained instead of voting for Švejnar, but Klaus fell one vote short of a majority of 140 of the 278 lawmakers present.<ref>Xinhua: [https://web.archive.org/web/20110514150524/http://news.xinhuanet.com/english/2008-02/10/content_7584740.htm Czech lawmakers fail to elect new president]</ref>

